PS5 HDMI: VRR test 19, on top of v1.5 (hdmi.vrr_test=1)     [ps5-bazzite-deck, parked]

Test 17 (VTEM SDP, test 16 queue-once re-setup, test 15 pre-block, ALLM,
DPCD dump, FreeSync InfoFrame) rebased onto the v1.5 kernel (USB-C port,
EDID handling, session-switch fixes), plus, after hsgodd's test 16/17
results (native path: VRR entered, picture up for a moment, then lost):
 - every ICC query/reply is kept; after the pre-block message its reply is
   logged, and if it passes stock's checks (service 0x10, reply[2..3]=0x4000,
   status reply[0xc]=0) and isn't our own bytes echoed, 0x7077 is written
   again from it (reply+0x14, 24 bits, / 100), as stock does after that reply
   (vrr_7077_reply, vrr_7077 still overrides)
 - then UPDCTRL (0x7011) bit 4 CLKUPD latches it (vrr_updctrl, 0 = off)
 - the VTEM SDP (test 17) is off by default (ruled out), vrr_vtem=1..4 still
Test 19 on top (hsgodd, decode of the stock builder at 0x4b3b20-0x4b3fa4 and
0x4b4a59): stock's first PHY message is ours plus a tail we never sent (selectors
0x19-0x3b with 0x7026/0x7024 values). There is no read command; the bridge answers
with the value in the reply, and stock takes 0x7077 from reply+0x14 (24 bits) / 100.
With hdmi.vrr_test=1 on FLAVA3 the tail is sent (vrr_phy_tail: 1 full, 2 only
0x1b/0x2b/0x3b, 0 none), that reply is logged and its value used for 0x7077
(stand-in pixel clock / 100 only as a fallback; the source is logged). Test 18's
rewrite from the pre-block reply (the wrong message) is log-only now.
